{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED — Gerrit change 1952 (Change-Id I335173422460423e9020792e4d777b6c6b047b34).\n\nTHE FIX. `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py` now builds its bare remote through\n`_init_bare_remote()`, which pins `_BARE_REMOTE_UPKEEP_PINS` before anything is pushed:\n\n    gc.autoDetach = false\n    maintenance.autoDetach = false\n    receive.autogc = false\n\nWHY THIS REMOVES THE RACE RATHER THAN NARROWING IT. The race exists because a push leaves a\nprocess running. `receive.autogc=false` means the push spawns no maintenance at all —\nmeasured, the push's `git maintenance run` child count drops from 1 to 0. The two\n`autoDetach` pins do not suppress maintenance; they force it FOREGROUND, so any other trigger\ncompletes before the git command returns. Under either pin the set of processes touching the\nbare repo when `copytree` starts is EMPTY, which is a structural property of the fixture, not\na probability. Nothing in the change retries, sleeps, sets a timing bound, filters `*.lock`,\nor relaxes an assertion.\n\nMeasured postures, all with `receive-pack` confirmed present in a `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` trace:\n\n  git defaults              -> 1 maintenance child, `--detach`     (background mutator)\n  autoDetach pins only      -> 1 maintenance child, `--no-detach`  (foreground, push waits)\n  all three pins            -> 0 maintenance children\n\nTHE NEW GUARD. Asserting the copy \"works\" cannot prove the mutator is gone — the race is a\ncoin flip, so a green copy is consistent with the mutator still existing. So\n`test_fixture_bare_remote_leaves_no_detached_upkeep_behind_a_push` asserts its ABSENCE from\ngit's own process trace: the push runs under `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` and no `git maintenance run`\nchild it spawns may carry `--detach`. A `receive-pack` positive control runs first, so the\nguard cannot pass against an empty or unwritten trace. Assertion is a content fact about an\nargv list; no timing bound, no polling.\n\nRED/GREEN PROVEN ON BOTH HALVES — not asserted as equivalent, actually run.\n\n1. The new guard discriminates. Seeded defect: `_BARE_REMOTE_UPKEEP_PINS` emptied to `{}`.\n   RED, with the mutator named in the failure:\n\n     AssertionError: the push left detached background upkeep running against\n     .../test_fixture_bare_remote_leave0/origin.git:\n     [['git', 'maintenance', 'run', '--auto', '--quiet', '--detach']]\n\n   Restored -> 13 passed.\n\n2. The EXISTING test still proves what it guards. Seeded defect: `_local_sibling_rewrites()`\n   in `tests/_topology_template.py` made to `return []`, so a copied store is never\n   re-pointed at its own copied sibling origin. RED on the test's OWN assertion:\n\n     AssertionError: the copied store still pushes to its template topology's origin\n     assert PosixPath('.../source/origin.git') == PosixPath('.../destination/origin.git')\n\n   Restored -> 13 passed. A second, harsher seed (all rewrites dropped AND the helper's own\n   `_assert_source_paths_absent` / `assert_store_self_contained` self-checks silenced) also\n   goes RED through this same assertion — it is the module's earliest tripwire, so the\n   ordering means this one assertion catches both seeds.\n\nGATES, run from the worktree venv:\n\n  make lint                                       exit 0\n  make typecheck                                  Success: no issues found in 582 source files\n  scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check    active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0\n  pytest tests/interfaces                         1947 passed, 10 skipped, 1 xfailed\n  pytest tests/unit                               11666 passed, 44 skipped\n\nThe two tiers were run in the FOREGROUND (a detached run has produced phantom errors before —\nsee nonodorous-snotty-seaurchin), and with Jira live env vars unset.\n\nSCOPE HELD. The survey found the same unpinned-bare-remote pattern at two further HIGH-risk\nsites — `tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py:140` and\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py:37`, both of which push into a bare remote\nthat `clone_topology_template` later copytrees AND byte-walks — plus ~35 latent MEDIUM sites.\nNone of them are touched by this change. They are filed as uneconomic-eastern-siskin\n(b394-6198-6010-42f7), linked `discovered_from` this ticket, with the full site list and the\nobservation that `clone_topology_template` is the amplifier worth hardening."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787207972058217001,"uuid":"69183ef9-a2a9-4ee4-89f6-b88843d54e21"}